<title>FRANCE: Schneider sold Sema shares.</title>
<headline>Schneider sold Sema shares.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French electrical distribution company Schneider said in a statement that it had sold 5.31 percent in Sema Group Plc, which it held through OSITEL, to institutional investors.</p>
<p>It said the private placement was carried out by HSBC James Capel.</p>
<p>It added the placement was in agreement with Sema, an Anglo-French information technology group.  </p>
<p>A spokesman for Schneider said the placement was carried out on Wednesday and represented the company's entire stake in SEMA.</p>
<p>He added that the company made a capital gain on the placement but he declined to give the price or the size of the gain.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
